Privacy Policy

Privacy Policy (Last Updated: June 2025)

At Grade Calculator, we prioritize your privacy and the protection of your academic information. This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, use, and safeguard your personal and academic data when you use our platform.

By using our services, you consent to the practices outlined here.

We collect: Name, USN, semester details, subjects, credits, internal marks, previous semester data for CGPA, usage data, and device/browser info.

We use your data to: Calculate SGPA/CGPA, generate reports, improve algorithms, provide support, and save history.

We secure your data via encryption (SSL/TLS), restricted access, secure databases, audits, and backups.

You have the right to access, correct, export, delete your data, or opt out of non-essential communications.

We do not sell your data. No academic data is shared without consent. Anonymous usage stats may be used for research. Data may be disclosed to comply with legal obligations or for operational purposes.

Data is retained while your account is active. Inactive accounts may be removed after 2 years with prior notice.

For privacy concerns: Email: Msv.innovation@gmail.com (Response time: 48 hours).

This policy may be updated. Updates will be posted with a revised date. Continued use means acceptance of changes.


